2026-06-05 05:58:57,203 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 1. **🔴 CRITICAL: Cross-System Credential Reuse (vibranium account)** — The `vibranium` domain account authenticated from BOTH compromised workstations (nromanoff at 15:34:48 and XP at 16:37:53 on 2012-04-04) to the domain controller. This definitively links the Snake/Uroburos malware on nromanoff and the spinlock.exe/pe.exe tools on XP to a **single threat actor**.
2026-06-05 05:58:57,205 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 2. **🔴 CRITICAL: Coordinated Multi-System APT Campaign** — A coherent 5-phase kill chain spanning 3 systems, established from 7 independent evidence sources (YARA, event logs, memory forensics, MFT, ShimCache, registry, file listings). The vibranium credential bridge is the definitive cross-system link.
2026-06-05 05:58:57,207 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 3. **🔴 CRITICAL: Classified Data Access Across Multiple Systems** — Undercover Agent Lists accessed from both the Snake-compromised nromanoff workstation and the DC via stolen vibranium credentials. Credit card data also accessed. Potential exfiltration via Snake's encrypted C2 or Dropbox on XP.
2026-06-05 05:58:57,210 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 4. **🔴 HIGH: Environment-Wide Defense Evasion** — Consistent timestomping (to OS build dates), binary masquerading, and process hiding across both DC and XP systems indicates a single operator with developed tradecraft.
2026-06-05 05:58:57,211 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 5. **🟡 MEDIUM: External SMTP Brute-Force is Independent** — The 91.207.6.58 attack is confirmed as separate from the APT campaign — different TTPs, no cross-system IOC overlap, all attempts failed.
2026-06-05 05:58:57,213 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 6. **🟡 MEDIUM: Anti-Forensic Tool (SDelete) on DC** — Evidence recovery may be impaired by SDelete presence alongside 11,973 deleted files.
