2026-06-05 06:02:54,364 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "investigation_questions": [
2026-06-05 06:02:54,364 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q1-CHALLENGE: Could the YARA web shell signatures on the DC memory be from McAfee's malware signature database (running McAfee ePO with Apache/Tomcat) rather than actual deployed web shells? The DC runs a full McAfee installation whose AV engine loads signature patterns into memory.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,365 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q2-CHALLENGE: Is the vibranium account a legitimate shared IT administration account? If vibranium was created as a domain admin service account before the incident window, the cross-system authentication pattern could reflect normal admin workflows rather than lateral movement.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,365 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q3-CHALLENGE: Could the PyInstaller Python 2.5 bundles under vibranium's temp directory be McAfee ePO management components? McAfee ePO historically used Python 2.x internally, and the _MEI* directories are standard PyInstaller extraction paths.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,366 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q4-CHALLENGE: Is the 96.255.98.154:29932 connection a legitimate remote management tool (TeamViewer, LogMeIn, GoToAssist) used by mhill.shield@yahoo.com for authorized remote admin? The same IP shows legitimate web browsing activity.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,366 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q5-CHALLENGE: Could SRL-Helpdesk's RDP session and the svchost.exe launch be a legitimate helpdesk technician running a system diagnostic utility? SRL-Helpdesk is an explicitly named IT support account.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,367 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q6-REVERSE: Does the 63-minute gap between vibranium authenticating from 10.3.58.5 (15:34:48) and 10.3.58.7 (16:37:53) on 2012-04-04 definitively prove single-operator credential reuse? This is the strongest link between the two compromised systems — no legitimate scenario easily explains a shared admin account authenticating from two DIFFERENT user workstations within an hour to access classified documents.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,368 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q7-REVERSE: Are the individually dismissable indicators (YARA Snake match on disk + web shells in memory + vibranium credential reuse + classified document access + spinlock C2 chain + timestomping to OS build dates + process hiding in pslist) forming convergent evidence that constitutes a confirmed APT intrusion when viewed as a unified chain?",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,368 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q8-REVERSE: Has the investigation adequately assessed the YARA Snake/Uroburos match quality? The rule matched at 7+ distinct offsets on the nromanoff disk with Snake-specific format strings (%s#1 through %s#4) and characteristic file extensions (.sav, .upd, .tmp). Multiple offset matches are inconsistent with a single false positive.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,369 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q9-COVERAGE: Why was YARA scanning not performed on the XP system (10.3.58.7) memory or disk? The XP system shows the most active C2 activity (spinlock.exe, pe.exe, dllhost\\svchost.exe). YARA could confirm or rule out known malware family attribution.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,369 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q10-DEDUP: Should findings be consolidated around attack phases rather than individual artifacts? Currently, spinlock.exe activity is spread across 8 findings, svchost.exe across 9, and vibranium across 6+. A single finding per attack phase (initial access, persistence, lateral movement, data access) would be clearer.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,370 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q11-CHALLENGE: Could F-Response forensic acquisition artifacts be contaminating the timeline? F-Response iSCSI connections, process injections, and network activity are forensic collection artifacts, not attack indicators. Verify no F-Response activity was misattributed.",
2026-06-05 06:02:54,370 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q12-REVERSE: The nfury system (10.3.58.6) showing NO compromise indicators alongside two heavily compromised adjacent systems (nromanoff 10.3.58.5, XP 10.3.58.7) — does this selectivity support a targeted APT hypothesis (selective compromise of systems with classified data access) rather than opportunistic malware spread?"
2026-06-05 06:02:54,371 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ],
